{
  "case_id": "2006-05-1284",
  "document_hash": "a933db2307ff86ec940adf65488243334cf3682a207a783be8cafa2c3804b4f7",
  "records": [
    {
      "attribution": "Court",
      "case_id": "2006-05-1284",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "a933db2307ff86ec940adf65488243334cf3682a207a783be8cafa2c3804b4f7",
      "evidence_id": "ev-a933db2307ff-0000-0000",
      "kind": "procedural_event",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 1,
        "start": 1
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "The above-entitled matter came on for oral argument before the Supreme Court of the United States at 11:18 a.m."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "United States (Amicus Curiae)",
      "case_id": "2006-05-1284",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "a933db2307ff86ec940adf65488243334cf3682a207a783be8cafa2c3804b4f7",
      "evidence_id": "ev-a933db2307ff-0000-0003",
      "kind": "amicus_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 19,
        "start": 19
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Manufacturers of cars, drugs, medical devices, pesticides, home appliances and numerous other consumer good market their products in accordance with detailed and specific Federal Government regulation."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "United States (Amicus Curiae)",
      "case_id": "2006-05-1284",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "a933db2307ff86ec940adf65488243334cf3682a207a783be8cafa2c3804b4f7",
      "evidence_id": "ev-a933db2307ff-0000-0006",
      "kind": "stated_consequence",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 19,
        "start": 19
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "If that in a colorable preemption defense were sufficient to trigger removal, then it would create the potential for a very major shift of traditional State law litigation from State to Federal court."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Scalia",
      "case_id": "2006-05-1284",
      "confidence": 0.99,
      "document_hash": "a933db2307ff86ec940adf65488243334cf3682a207a783be8cafa2c3804b4f7",
      "evidence_id": "ev-a933db2307ff-0001-0000",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 20,
        "start": 20
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE SCALIA: Yeah, but is there some Government official who's there to make sure that the testing is being done the way, the way it's supposed to be, which is what, what is argued is the case here?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Government",
      "case_id": "2006-05-1284",
      "confidence": 0.9,
      "document_hash": "a933db2307ff86ec940adf65488243334cf3682a207a783be8cafa2c3804b4f7",
      "evidence_id": "ev-a933db2307ff-0001-0001",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 20,
        "start": 20
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "MR. GORNSTEIN: Policing and enforcing the testing requirements, and there's testing in all these areas. The other thing to say is that there's no --"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Chief Justice Roberts",
      "case_id": "2006-05-1284",
      "confidence": 0.99,
      "document_hash": "a933db2307ff86ec940adf65488243334cf3682a207a783be8cafa2c3804b4f7",
      "evidence_id": "ev-a933db2307ff-0001-0002",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 21,
        "start": 21
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "CHIEF JUSTICE ROBERTS: What about -- what about USDA food inspection? Isn't a lot of that delegated to the producers rather than the Government officials?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Mr. Olson",
      "case_id": "2006-05-1284",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "a933db2307ff86ec940adf65488243334cf3682a207a783be8cafa2c3804b4f7",
      "evidence_id": "ev-a933db2307ff-0002-0000",
      "kind": "allegation",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 38,
        "start": 38
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "becomes the FTC official ratings which they then must transmit to the company in their advertising. And now they're sued because those ratings that they've done according, for the FTC, according to the FTC standards, are alleged to be misleading."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Breyer",
      "case_id": "2006-05-1284",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "a933db2307ff86ec940adf65488243334cf3682a207a783be8cafa2c3804b4f7",
      "evidence_id": "ev-a933db2307ff-0002-0001",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 38,
        "start": 38
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "All right. So what you are saying is that this function is so separable and it is so much a FTC function and it is so much like delegating it to the third party that did nothing of the testing, that even if you delegate it to the second party which does testing and then benefits from the testing, that's still not enough to take it out."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Breyer",
      "case_id": "2006-05-1284",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "a933db2307ff86ec940adf65488243334cf3682a207a783be8cafa2c3804b4f7",
      "evidence_id": "ev-a933db2307ff-0002-0002",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 39,
        "start": 39
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Then is there any, any authority ever, that you found for that?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Mr. Olson",
      "case_id": "2006-05-1284",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "a933db2307ff86ec940adf65488243334cf3682a207a783be8cafa2c3804b4f7",
      "evidence_id": "ev-a933db2307ff-0002-0003",
      "kind": "fact",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 40,
        "start": 40
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "This is, as the Eighth Circuit said, a very unusual situation. But the closest analogies are, are to the Government contractor cases. And by the way, it doesn't require a contract to be acting under the supervision. I heard the Government say that what you had to have is someone supervised by the Government with the Government's power to alter the actor's conduct."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Roberts",
      "case_id": "2006-05-1284",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "a933db2307ff86ec940adf65488243334cf3682a207a783be8cafa2c3804b4f7",
      "evidence_id": "ev-a933db2307ff-0002-0005",
      "kind": "fact",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 43,
        "start": 43
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "the complaint in this case, testing is a small part of it. They're complaining about the modification of the tobacco blend, the weight, rod length, the circumference, use of reconstituted tobacco sheets. In other words there's a lot going on here in the complaint here besides the testing."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Mr. Olson",
      "case_id": "2006-05-1284",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "a933db2307ff86ec940adf65488243334cf3682a207a783be8cafa2c3804b4f7",
      "evidence_id": "ev-a933db2307ff-0002-0006",
      "kind": "allegation",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 44,
        "start": 44
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "misleading low tar and nicotine ratings as measured by the company's testing procedures. That's in the Petitioners' motion to remand."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Breyer",
      "case_id": "2006-05-1284",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "a933db2307ff86ec940adf65488243334cf3682a207a783be8cafa2c3804b4f7",
      "evidence_id": "ev-a933db2307ff-0002-0008",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 46,
        "start": 46
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "I have a quick question."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Breyer",
      "case_id": "2006-05-1284",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "a933db2307ff86ec940adf65488243334cf3682a207a783be8cafa2c3804b4f7",
      "evidence_id": "ev-a933db2307ff-0002-0009",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 47,
        "start": 47
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Is there anything in the complaint that alleges you didn't perform the tests properly?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Mr. Olson",
      "case_id": "2006-05-1284",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "a933db2307ff86ec940adf65488243334cf3682a207a783be8cafa2c3804b4f7",
      "evidence_id": "ev-a933db2307ff-0002-0010",
      "kind": "fact",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 48,
        "start": 48
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "the core, the heart of the lawsuit, as the district court said and the Eighth Circuit said is, you're doing what the FTC required you to do, and the plaintiffs say that it's deceptive."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Breyer",
      "case_id": "2006-05-1284",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "a933db2307ff86ec940adf65488243334cf3682a207a783be8cafa2c3804b4f7",
      "evidence_id": "ev-a933db2307ff-0002-0011",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 49,
        "start": 49
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Is it the apple institute who's doing the testing?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Mr. Olson",
      "case_id": "2006-05-1284",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "a933db2307ff86ec940adf65488243334cf3682a207a783be8cafa2c3804b4f7",
      "evidence_id": "ev-a933db2307ff-0002-0012",
      "kind": "fact",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 50,
        "start": 50
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "This case comes down to the fact that the FTC wanted certain things done. It decided how certain things would be done. It calls the results of those the official FTC ratings. It wants those ratings delivered to the people."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Source extraction",
      "case_id": "2006-05-1284",
      "confidence": 0.0,
